speechtext:
I wish to add my protest against the grants to class B fairs being cut down or taken off altogether. These fairs are doing about as much good as any other fairs;

Supply-Agriculture-Exhibitions
they are doing a lot more good than the smaller class C fairs, and their work is equally valuable to that done by the class A fairs. According to the minister's figures the class A fairs receive $85,000 per year, while the class B fairs have been receiving about $33,000. That covered twenty-two fairs, which are doing educational work as valuable as that done by any otheir fairs, and there is not the slightest doubt that if this grant is cut down or taken off altogether many of these fairs will be forced to drop to class C, and will be unable to continue with the valuable educational work they are doing at present Therefore I would ask the minister to reconsider his decision, and if he cannot give the amount given in past years let him at least give part of it. If he cannot continue the grant for any length of time let him tell this house for how many years he can continue it, in order to give these fair boards all over the country an opportunity gradually to adjust themselves to this condition.
